<title>USA: Shoemaker Kani Inc postpones IPO - underwriter.</title>
<headline>Shoemaker Kani Inc postpones IPO - underwriter.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kani Inc, a company licensed to sell shoes under the Karl Kani brand name, has postponed its planned initial public offering, the lead underwriter said on Monday.</p>
<p>Lead underwriter Joseph Charles Inc would not provide the reasons behind the postponement.</p>
<p>The Manhattan Beach, California, company was due to offer 1.4 million shares in a range of $10 to $12 each. The company filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for the offering in October 1996.</p>
</text>
